      "assessment": "Integer-ladder arithmetic has two Pythagorean triples sharing one leg and uses Euclidean primitive triples and gcd. It imposes an integer crossing-height condition pq/(p+q), not the P11 base relation P=A+B,Q=|A-B|, the (11,8) fixed-core elliptic point, or sixteen recovered-root normalization. Its finite enumeration does not duplicate the all-n fixed-core P11 reconstruction proof."
